  "checks": [
    "All eleven current source and object hashes equal their strict-receipt bindings; all three receipt audit sources/logs rehashed; all 41 declarations printed once in exact declared order and have exactly propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound in their transitive reports.",
    "v5 includes the same-line attributed pairCenterEquiv_apply previously missed by v3 discovery. Existing support v3 receipts have no analogous selection omission. Historical receipts remain unchanged.",
    "pairCenterEquiv identifies the three spectator coordinates with the unscaled physical center t. pairCoordinates(r,t) gives x0=t+r/2 and x1=t-r/2; pairKSLift substitutes r=KS(y), so the pair radius is ||y||^2.",
    "The bilinear trace identity cancels mixed terms without Hessian symmetry: 4 Delta_r + Delta_t = 2 Delta_physical. KS therefore gives Delta_y + ||y||^2 Delta_t = 2||y||^2 Delta_physical, exactly Grushin c=1.",
    "Combining Delta g=2(V-E)g with the principal identity yields coefficient 4||y||^2(V-E). Its regular extension is 4+4||y||^2[-Z(1/|x0|+1/|x1|)-E], with value +4 on y=0 from electron repulsion.",
    "The coefficient patch excludes both nuclear positions but includes pair collision at nonzero center. Classical smoothness is only invoked with y nonzero and collisionFree. No smoothness at pair collision is assumed.",
    "Global pullbacks are compositions of actual continuous or locally Lipschitz representatives. No arbitrary L2 equivalence class is composed through a dimension-changing map, and no unproved pair-coordinate volume equivalence is used by this classical/weak route.",
    "The scaled integration-by-parts support accepts general real c. The conditional kernel implication derives both integrability and zero integral from a genuine local classical equation; parent Coulomb modules discharge that premise.",
    "Removability uses the codimension-four y-hole argument for continuous u and the smooth coefficient on the actual patch, with parameter c=1. It requires no derivative of u at y=0. Both integrability of the final weak integrand and its zero integral are conclusions.",
    "The full spin wrapper starts from the actual fermionic Hamiltonian eigen-graph, constructs one simultaneous locally Lipschitz representative family with a common almost-everywhere set and simultaneous spatial/spin permutation law, then applies the scalar pair result to each component.",
    "Factor-coordinate calculus avoids identifying the ordinary product max norm with an Euclidean inner-product norm."
